// Semantic / vector search over team play-style narratives.
// Paste into Kibana Dev Tools Console (ES|QL tab) to run.
//
// `narrative` is a semantic_text field (see mappings/nba_team_stats.json) --
// Elastic auto-embeds it with the deployment's default EIS model at index
// time. MATCH() against a semantic_text field runs a semantic (vector)
// search under the hood, not a keyword match -- so this finds teams whose
// play style matches the query's MEANING, not its exact words.
//
// Example: searching "lockdown defense and playing hot right now" can match
// a team whose narrative says "elite two-way team on a hot streak" even
// though none of the query words appear verbatim.
//
// IMPORTANT -- sort by _score, not by a stat. An earlier version of this
// query ended with `SORT net_rating DESC`, which silently discarded the
// semantic ranking: the rows came back ordered by how good each team is,
// not by how well it matched the description. That also made the obvious
// test ("search for a hot defensive team, confirm Boston ranks above New
// York") impossible to fail, since Boston has the higher net_rating and
// would sort first even if semantic search returned nothing useful.
// Requesting METADATA _score and sorting on it is what makes this a real
// relevance query -- and what makes the test meaningful.

FROM nba_team_stats METADATA _score
| WHERE MATCH(narrative, "lockdown defense and playing hot right now")
| KEEP team, narrative, _score, net_rating, last_10_wins, last_10_losses
| SORT _score DESC
| LIMIT 10

// --- How to tell it actually worked ---
//
// Run it a second time with a description that inverts the meaning but
// shares most of its vocabulary:
//
//   MATCH(narrative, "struggling defensively and losing at home lately")
//
// A real semantic match flips the order -- the team whose narrative
// describes a rough stretch should now rank first, and the _score values
// should differ noticeably between the two runs. If the order and scores
// barely move between the two queries, MATCH() is falling back to keyword
// behaviour and the embedding isn't being used. Check that the narrative
// field really is mapped as semantic_text (GET nba_team_stats/_mapping) and
// that the documents were indexed AFTER that mapping was applied -- docs
// indexed against an older mapping are not retroactively embedded.

// --- Fallback (Query DSL) ---
// If your Elastic version's ES|QL MATCH() doesn't yet support semantic_text
// fields, run this equivalent semantic query in Dev Tools instead. It sorts
// by relevance by default, so there's nothing extra to add:
//
// GET nba_team_stats/_search
// {
//   "query": {
//     "semantic": {
//       "field": "narrative",
//       "query": "lockdown defense and playing hot right now"
//     }
//   }
// }
